# O Come, All Ye Faithful, strum and sing (repertoire plan: o-come-all-ye-faithful). The hymn tune
# Adeste Fideles in G major with verse 1 of Frederick Oakeley's English words. Your part: five
# chords from the key of G, G (320003), C (x32010), D (xx0232), Em (022000) and Am (x02210),
# strummed four to the bar through the verse. The refrain line "O come, let us adore him" comes
# three times and the strumming builds: half notes, softly, the first time; quarters the second
# time; down, down-up on every beat the third time. The tune (second track) carries the words.
# A new arrangement for this app: the chords and strumming are not taken from any hymnal.
title: O Come, All Ye Faithful
id: o-come-all-ye-faithful
composer: John Francis Wade; English words by Frederick Oakeley
source: Hymn tune Adeste Fideles (John Francis Wade, c. 1751); English words by Frederick Oakeley (1841), verse 1; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Wade died in 1786, Oakeley in 1880); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: christmas, carol, strumming, lyrics
tempo: 88
time: 4/4
key: G
pickup: q

